# shipping.config — THE SHIPPING CONFIGURATION, IN ONE PLACE.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# On 2026-09-09 the build that ships was found not to be the build that was
# measured, in three independent parameters at once (findings S8-2, S9-1):
#
#   * BLOCK.  PW ruled on 2026-09-03 that block 16 is the configuration that
#     fits both chips -- block 8 is 116.4 % of chip 1's budget and 104.9 % of
#     chip 2's and never fitted either. The ruling was applied only inside the
#     measurement scripts, which build a scratch tree with DSP4_GEN_BLOCK=16.
#     The committed tree has been generated at BLOCK=8 since 2026-08-28 and
#     `./build.sh` has always produced a block-8 image.
#   * BLOCK KERNELS.  Every capacity figure since 2026-09-01, the `.4` record
#     included, is a DSP4_BLOCK_KERNELS=1 build. The build default was 0.
#   * CORE CLOCK.  Every cycle budget since 2026-08-24 is quoted at 983.04 MHz
#     on the strength of PW's U5/U6 part reading (ADSP-21564KSWZ10, the 1 GHz
#     grade). The build default was DSP4_CCLK_TARGET=0, which leaves the CGU on
#     its reset divisors at 491.52 MHz -- HALF the clock every budget assumes.
#     Read off the running window pair on 2026-09-09: CGU0_CTL 0x00002800 on
#     both chips, which is the reset row, not the 983.04 row (0x00005000).
#
# The consequence was measured, not inferred: the shipping per-sample block-8
# image misses 75.1 % of blocks on chip 1 and 70.9 % on chip 2, and a half
# that is not rewritten is transmitted again, so the wire carries stale whole
# blocks. No capacity number, latency figure or family walk could see it,
# because they were all taken on a different build.
#
# So the parameters that decide whether the loop fits the block live HERE, and
# nowhere else. `./build.sh` reads this file, `tools/dsp/dsp_codegen.py` reads
# this file for DSP4_GEN_BLOCK, and build.sh REFUSES to build a source tree
# whose generated dsp_block.h disagrees with it. An environment variable still
# overrides any line here -- that is how the control arms are built -- but the
# override is then explicit, in one command, and shows up in the image's own
# DIAG_BUILD_CFG word.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE, one per line, '#' comments. Parsed by shell (`source`)
# and by Python (tools/dsp/build_config.py). Values must be plain integers.

# ---- the four that decide whether the block loop fits the block ----

# Samples per DMA block. The whole tree is generated from this: every loop
# count, slot array, DMA ring, ramp step, meter coefficient and verdict rate.
# PW ruling 2026-09-03. Changing it means regenerating the tree, not editing
# dsp_block.h -- see tools/dsp/dsp_codegen.py.
DSP4_GEN_BLOCK=16

# One call per node per block with the sample loop inside the kernel, instead
# of one call per node per sample. Chip 1 330,389 -> 134,325 cycles/block,
# chip 2 286,757 -> 170,622, measured 2026-09-09 at block 8.
DSP4_BLOCK_KERNELS=1

# The ping/pong phase fix (src/sport_init.asm). The core used to start on the
# half the DDE was already clocking out, so every transmitted window was
# spliced from two or three consecutive blocks. 100.0000 % ordered on the part
# with it, 33 % without.
DSP4_BLK_LATCH=1

# Core clock. 983 = 983.040 MHz, legal on the ADSP-21564KSWZ10 fitted at
# U5/U6 (PW read the marking 2026-08-24) and OUT OF SPEC on a KSWZ8. This is
# the clock every cycle budget on this project is quoted at; a build with 0
# runs at 491.52 MHz and has half the budget it is being scored against.
DSP4_CCLK_TARGET=983

# ---- the rest of the shipping configuration, stated so it is not implicit ----

DSP4_BISECT=0             # 0 = production; anything else PARKS the firmware
DSP4_BLOCK_MASK=7         # 1 scatter | 2 node graph | 4 gather; 7 = whole loop
DSP4_CHAN_MASK=1          # CFG_CHAN_MASK/CFG_AUX_MASK have readers: a D24 runs 24 strips
DSP4_SCOPE_GATE=1         # skip nodes scoped to the other product at the dispatch table
DSP4_BQ_FLOAT=1           # the float landing, 2026-09-03
DSP4_BQ_ROUNDONCE=1       # per-stage saturate deleted, error feedback kept (PW, 2026-09-02)
# DSP4_BQ_GUARD is DERIVED, not set: dsp_block.h forces it to 0 whenever
# DSP4_BQ_FLOAT is on, because the float cascades are guard-free. Setting it
# here would be a line that does not describe the image -- the part read back
# 0 with this file saying 1, which is exactly the check DIAG_BUILD_CFG is for.
# ---- the two switches the capacity record was quoting and this file
# ---- did not name (findings S11-1, settled S12) -- SIGNED BY PW 2026-09-20
#
# PW SIGNED THE SIMD PAIRING CONFIGURATION ON 2026-09-20 ("sign it"), and
# these two are the pair of it. They are 1 here from S82 on. What the
# signature covers is four switches together -- DSP4_SIMD_DYN,
# DSP4_STRIP_FUSED, DSP4_DYN_LUT and DSP4_GATE_LINTHR -- with three accepted
# numeric bounds carried into the contract beside them; see the DYN_LUT /
# GATE_LINTHR section below for the bounds and MW/D24/DSP/s82/signed.md for
# the bar they were re-measured on.
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE EXISTS FOR APPLIED TO ITSELF. Every capacity figure
# from 2026-09-01 to 2026-09-09 was taken by the profile scripts, which
# force both of these to 1; build.sh defaults both to 0; this file named
# neither. Read against the shipping pair the two instruments disagreed by
# 78,245 cycles/block on chip 2 at D24 and 108,331 at D32 -- 24 % and 33 %
# of budget -- and the record could not say which number was the product
# (S10-6). They are named here now, at the value the image that SHIPS is
# built with, so that gap can never reopen: an arm that wants them on says
# so on its command line and the image's own DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 word says so
# back.
#
# WHAT THEY ARE WORTH, measured on the part 2026-09-09, D32 all-ones mask:
# together they take chip 2 from 112.7 % of budget to 82.03 % avg /
# 86.75 % worst with zero missed blocks over 270,082 -- D32 FITS with them
# and does not without. STRIP_FUSED alone is 3,542 cycles (1.08 %) and is
# PROVEN (famverify verdict-for-verdict identical to shipping, three
# numeric arms BIT_EXACT). SIMD_DYN is the other 97,092 cycles (29.6 %).
#
# Turning either of them on for the product is PW's ruling, not this
# file's: see MW/D32/DSP/dsp4-simd-dyn-s12-20260909.md for the decision
# table and what still stands against SIMD_DYN.

# Fused strip kernels -- intermediates kept in registers and the MAC
# accumulator instead of round-tripping through memory. Block-kernel
# builds only. 3,542 cycles/block (1.08 %) on chip 2, and PROVEN: famverify
# verdict-for-verdict identical to the unfused shipping pair, three numeric
# arms BIT_EXACT.
DSP4_STRIP_FUSED=1

# Paired (SIMD) dynamics and biquads: GATE/COMP -- and, through the
# derived DSP4_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH / DSP4_C2_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH, FILT/EQ and
# chip 2's aux and main biquads -- run two channels in one instruction
# stream. Also wires the odd block pool and the pair-ordered chain.
# 97,092 cycles/block (29.6 %) on chip 2 at D32. Bus-word-identical to the
# scalar graph: S20-6 captured 256 words of _buf_C1_BUS_MAIN_L on the paired
# and the scalar arm and got THE SAME CAPTURE BYTE FOR BYTE.
DSP4_SIMD_DYN=1

# THE TWO SWITCHES DSP4_SIMD_DYN IMPLIES, NAMED RATHER THAN IMPLIED.
# build.sh defaults DSP4_SIMD_GRAPH to 1 and derives DSP4_SIMD_STRIPS from
# DSP4_SIMD_DYN, so before S82 the signed configuration reached the image
# through two build.sh defaults and this file said nothing about either.
# That is the S8-2/S9-1/S76/S79 shape for the fifth time, and the whole
# point of this file. dsp_block.h computes DSP4_PAIRED_GRAPH from
# DSP4_SIMD_DYN && DSP4_SIMD_GRAPH, so SIMD_GRAPH=0 would put the paired
# kernels in the image and never call them.
DSP4_SIMD_GRAPH=1         # the paired CHAIN, not just the paired kernels
DSP4_SIMD_STRIPS=1        # one pool slot to park strip N's block for the pair

# ---- THE TWO DECLARED NUMERIC DEVIATIONS, SIGNED BY PW 2026-09-20 ----
#
# These two are not capacity levers that happen to be bit-exact; they are
# the only two switches in this file that CHANGE THE AUDIO by a stated
# amount. S20-6 is the measurement that isolates them: with both off and
# everything else in this configuration on, `busgold.sh` reproduces the
# 2026-08-30 golden capture BIT FOR BIT (0 of 256 words); with both on,
# 235 of 256 words differ and the worst word is 0.03934 dB. So the entire
# audible difference the signed configuration makes is these two lines, and
# it is inside the bounds below.
#
# THE THREE ACCEPTED BOUNDS ARE PART OF THE CONTRACT (PW, 2026-09-20). They
# are stated here, carried in proposals/CONTRACT-PROPOSAL-S82.md for the hub
# to land in defs/docs, and they are what the D24 acceptance fixtures score:
#
#   DSP4_DYN_LUT       <= 0.0950 dB   design bound over the documented sweep
#   DSP4_GATE_LINTHR   <= 0.0002 dB   effective-threshold shift
#   COMPRESSOR numeric <= 0.00518 dB  one verdict of famverify's twenty
#                                     moves numerically, by this much
#
# A measurement outside its bound is a STOP, not a re-signing.

# The COMPRESSOR's and LIMITER's whole static curve -- threshold, ratio,
# knee, ceiling -- baked into a per-node table by a DESIGN step that runs
# only when a parameter moves. The per-sample gain computer becomes an index,
# two words and an interpolation: 215.2 -> 54.1 cycles per sample-pair
# (74.9 %), the whole compressor body 284.3 -> 123.1. Costs 337 words of DM
# per COMPRESSOR and LIMITER node at the shipped K = 4, and 0.0950 dB worst
# case against PW's 0.1 dB ruling of 2026-09-09 -- tools/dsp/dyn_lut_design.py
# PRODUCES that number, it is not remembered here.
DSP4_DYN_LUT=1

# GATE threshold compared in the linear domain instead of log2: one
# _log2q_fx call per sample deleted. The gate's effective threshold shifts by
# at most 0.0002 dB, which is the deviation PW signed.
DSP4_GATE_LINTHR=1

# NOT SIGNED, AND IT MUST STAY 0 FOR A SECOND REASON. DSP4_DYN_TABLES is a
# third numeric deviation (0.000016 / 0.000008 dB -- MORE accurate than the
# polynomial it replaces, and still a deviation), and it is INCOMPATIBLE with
# DSP4_SIMD_DYN: a table lookup is a gather at two indices and the DAGs are
# shared, so the assembler refuses the combination. With the pairing signed,
# this line is now load-bearing rather than a placeholder.
DSP4_DYN_TABLES=0

# Chip 2's AUX and MAIN biquads paired (derived: only takes effect when
# DSP4_SIMD_DYN is on, through DSP4_C2_BQ_PAIRED_GRAPH).
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-10 (findings S20-2). THE TWO REASONS THIS COMMENT GAVE
# FOR THE 0 ARE BOTH OUT OF DATE, and they were out of date for a day in the
# one file that exists to be the single source of truth about the shipping
# build -- which is the fault this file exists for, appearing in its own
# prose instead of its own values.
#
# It used to say "NAMED HERE AT 0 BECAUSE IT IS NOT AUDIO-CORRECT (findings
# S12-5)". That defect -- a band gain written into a paired AUX GEQ and a
# notch gain written into a paired AUX AFB never becoming coefficients at
# all, on 18 of the 24 chip-2 pairs -- was ROOT-CAUSED AND FIXED the next
# day: S13-1, status CLOSED. The pair driver's steady test never read the
# pending-DESIGN flag, so for any class the host writes PARAMETERS to (GEQ
# band gains, AFB notches, crossover corners) the design step at the top of
# the node body -- the body the latch exists to skip -- never ran,
# swap_pending never rose and the pair ran its .var bypass initialisers for
# ever. Fixed in tools/dsp/dsp_codegen.py::gen_bq_pairs_c2; witnessed by
# geqverify and afbverify at 1-4 ulp (against 50.9 M / 83.9 M before),
# famverify GEQ and ANTI_FB LIVE paired moved 64/64, and bqeverify 0 ulp
# over 36,864 words.
#
# It also used to say "DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 does NOT carry this bit, so the two
# candidate images read back the same word and differ in audio (S12-7)".
# S15-9 put it in bit 12 of that word and S18-4 taught the bench decoder to
# read it; S12-7 is CLOSED. An s20 image reads back 0xC2011E4F and says so.
#
# SO THE 0 HERE IS NOW A RULING AND NOT A DEFECT. It stays 0 until PW moves
# it, and MW/D32/DSP/SHARC/shipping.config.s20 is the proposal to move it --
# with the driven capacity table that makes the case
# (MW/D32/DSP/dsp4-s20-20260910.md). It costs capacity to leave it off: on
# chip 2 at D32 it is worth about twenty points.
DSP4_C2_BQ_GRAPH=0

# ---- THE CODE-POOL LEVER (S16/S18/S21/S26, LANDED S76) ----
#
# COMP, TUBE, GATE and FILT stop being emitted 32 times each. Each class's
# nodes become a per-node stub that puts that strip's record base in i7 (and
# its predecessor's scalar buffer in i5, and for FILT its block-pool slot in
# i6) and jumps to ONE body in chip1/shared_kernels.asm. Mask 15 = all four.
#
# THIS LINE DID NOT EXIST UNTIL S76, WHICH IS THE FAULT THIS FILE EXISTS FOR.
# The switch was at build.sh's default of 0 and nothing named it, while every
# fit table since S20 priced it at 15 (shipping.config.s20/.s21/.s26/.s32) --
# the same shape as findings S8-2/S9-1, one directory down.
#
# WHAT IT BUYS, measured on the map each build produced (S76 gate 1):
#
#   chip 1 code, shipping arm   253,238 -> 157,590 of 262,144
#                               96.6 % -> 60.1 %, 8,906 B free -> 104,554
#   chip 1 code, EXTRAM arm     261,198 -> 165,550
#                               99.6 % -> 63.2 %, 946 B free -> 96,594
#
# Accounted to the byte: GATE -30,592, COMP -29,696, FILT -28,352,
# TUBE -10,176, the one shared body +3,168, total -95,648. Nothing is
# removed -- 32 copies of a kernel become one -- so S22 completeness is
# untouched. Chip 2 has no strip COMP, TUBE, GATE or FILT and is unaffected:
# its .ldr differs from S74c's in EXACTLY TWO BYTES, which are bits 5 and 15
# of its own DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 stamp saying this switch is on.
#
# AUDIO: bit-exact, and proved on the MACHINE CODE rather than argued.
# `tools/dsp/shk_equiv.py` disassembles both arms and requires, for all 128
# nodes of the four classes, the same instruction sequence touching the same
# ABSOLUTE addresses -- the shared body's `dm(0x25,i7)` resolved through what
# that node's stub loaded, against the inline arm's `dm(_comp_cgp_C1_COMP_01)`
# resolved through the linker. 128/128 on both arms. The harness is not
# vacuous: `--mutate` shifts one node's record base by one word and the run
# must fail, which it does (48 divergences on that node, none elsewhere).
# The ONE difference it does allow is named and bounded: FILT's four-
# instruction `l3/l4/i3/i4` prologue is hoisted out of the crossfade branch
# into the stub, so it runs on every block instead of only on crossfade
# blocks; nothing reads any of those four registers before the point the
# inline arm sets them.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS: a jump and the stub's register loads, per node per block.
# See MW/D24/DSP/s76/capacity.md for the static count and the measured shk
# sweep; it is NOT re-measured driven on the part in S76 (desk session).
DSP4_SHARED_KERNELS=15

# ---- S9-2 Option A, ADOPTED (PW ruling 2026-09-09 14:3x) ----
#
# Transmit a half early. The core fills the DMA half the DDE is NOT
# clocking, so a block's outputs are complete a whole period before frame 0
# of that half goes on the wire; this removes the deadline rather than
# buying margin against it. Measured on the part 2026-09-09 (S11,
# `dsp4-s92-optionA-20260909.md`): 100.0000 % ordered at full load with the
# Pi staircase, ONE entry in the histogram, for ZERO cycles and ZERO DM --
# there is no staging block, the core writes the half it is not clocking.
#
# A PER-CHIP MASK because the cost is per chip: 1 = chip 1's inter-chip TX,
# 2 = chip 2's converter TX, 3 = both. PW ruled CHIP 2 ONLY. It costs
# +16 samples of output latency, so the through-DSP figure is 82 samples /
# 1.708 ms at block 16 and that is the contract number -- see the window
# note. Chip 1's inter-chip TX still has the same defect and the stamp
# cannot see it; that is recorded, not fixed.
#
# Requires DSP4_BLK_LATCH (src/sport_init.asm says so at assembly time) and
# DSP4_GATHER_FIRST stays on beside it -- with GATHER_FIRST off the same arm
# reads 98.2156 % and chip 2 misses 2.7 % of blocks.
DSP4_TX_EARLY=2

# ---- THE SELF-TEST NODES (S49) ----
#
# TEST_OSC + TEST_MEAS, the graph nodes behind the `Test[1-1]*` cell family:
# a sine oscillator injectable into any strip's input block and an
# RMS / THD+N / noise / crosstalk engine reading any strip's post-fader
# block. Chip 1 only; chip 2 carries not one instruction of it and rebuilds
# BYTE FOR BYTE at this value (7b1311e8e56f008fa98046cab59293c6, the S42
# chip-2 image).
#
# 0 IS NOT A DEFECT AND IT IS NOT A CONTROL ARM EITHER -- it is a PENDING
# RULING. The nodes work on the part (MW/D24/DSP/dsp4-s49-20260915.md): they
# measured the D24 channel strip flat to +-0.01 dB from 100 Hz to 20 kHz at
# a THD+N floor of -103 to -141 dB, read the compressor's own 4:1 knee off
# its transfer curve, and agreed with an independent host-side FFT to 0.00 dB
# on level and on THD+N. What stands against turning them on is CHIP 1's
# HEADROOM, not the nodes:
#
#   carrying them, idle:  below the instrument's own resolution. The
#                         cross-boot spread on code that did not change at
#                         all (chip 2) is ~2,000 cycles/block, and the
#                         chip-1 idle difference is inside it. Bounded from
#                         the code at ~640 cycles/block, 0.2 % of budget:
#                         64 hook sites x ~10 cycles.
#   USING them:           +1,520 cycles/block average, +903 worst-block,
#                         measured on ONE boot with one cell write between
#                         the two readings -- 0.46 % / 0.28 % of budget.
#
# Against a chip 1 sitting at 98.1 % of budget with zero missed blocks, that
# is affordable; whether a shipping image should carry a test oscillator at
# all is PW's call and not this file's. Turning it on also needs the
# `Test[1-1]*` addresses landed -- see proposals/CONTRACT-PROPOSAL-S49.md --
# because without them no host can reach the cells.
DSP4_TEST_NODES=0

# THE CUE BUS (S65, src/chip1/cue.asm + src/chip2/cue_rx.asm): the stereo
# cue sum on chip 1, MIX_2 slots 9/10 to chip 2's monitor (source 13), cells
# proposed at chip-1 SPI 0x1378.. (proposals/CONTRACT-PROPOSAL-S65.md).
# 0 here = both images are byte-identical to the tree without it.
DSP4_CUE=0

# THE RTA FILTERBANK (S64; chip 1 since S65, src/chip1/rta.asm): 31 x
# 1/3-octave x 3 biquads x 2 channels with fast/slow/peak ballistics on the
# cue bus, after chip 1's chain, armed by RtaOn. Needs DSP4_CUE=1. Cost on
# chip 1: findings S65. 0 here = the image is byte-identical without it.
DSP4_RTA=0

DSP4_TALK_INVERT=1        # talkback polarity flip (S71); ON (S74, PW ruling
                          # 2026-09-19 evening: "tb polarity can be signed in
                          # code") -- ships inverted-corrected
# THE EXTERNAL-RAM DELAY POOL (S75). PW ruling 2026-09-19 evening: "dsp ram
# is required, but needs to work without it until dsp board modified -- code
# it in place." One 64 Mbit 3.0 V HyperRAM per ADSP-21564 on xSPI0 carries the
# delay history; the L2 ring stays as the head window and the tail is staged
# by MDMA in whole blocks (src/mem_pool.asm, src/extram.asm).
#
# 0 IS NOT A CONTROL ARM AND NOT A PENDING RULING -- IT IS THE ONLY VALUE THE
# HARDWARE ALLOWS TODAY. No DSP4 card has the part fitted, and two hardware
# questions stand before one can (MW/D24/DSP/s75/extram-pool.md, S75-1 and
# S75-2: octal xSPI0 takes the Pi parameter link's pins and the boot port's
# with them, and both candidate part numbers read as the 1.8 V variants of a
# 3.3 V-only I/O domain). At 0 the pool and the whole xSPI layer emit not one
# byte: the shipping pair rebuilds BYTE-IDENTICAL to S74c's, checked, not
# asserted.
#
# A THIRD BLOCKER LIVES IN THIS TREE AND IS CHEAP: the DSP4_EXTRAM=1 arm
# leaves chip 1 with 942 bytes of program memory free (99.6 % of the code
# pool). Code reclamation comes before this moves. Finding S75-5.
#
# In DIAG_BUILD_CFG3 bit 0 -- a NEW word, because diag.h's own note says the
# next flag of this class needs one rather than a seventh narrowing of CFG2's
# signature. S80 filled the rest of that word and made its DM cell
# unconditional, so 0xE0EC answers on every image now and not only on an
# EXTRAM one. Turning this on does not turn the RAM on: the image still probes
# at boot and still falls back to L2 when nothing answers, and which backend
# it actually chose is the RUNTIME word DIAG_EXTRAM_STAT.
DSP4_EXTRAM=0

DSP4_TXPROBE=0            # bench instrument only; never in a shipping image
DSP4_PROFILE_SIGNAL=0     # measurement arm only

# The stuck-partial-request recovery, armed only while the parameter link is
# standing still (D71, and D79 with it -- diag.asm:721 is the ONLY place in the
# firmware that discards a single word, and an unconditional discard during the
# host's 51-transaction config burst puts every later request a word out of
# phase). build.sh has defaulted this to 1 since 2026-08-31; naming it here
# makes the shipping position stated rather than implicit.
DSP4_SPI_PARTIAL_FIX2=1

# ---- THE OFF-AUX PARK GATE (S32, landed in the SHIPPING file at S79) ----
#
# Twelve chip-2 `AUX_INPUT` nodes — `C2_SNK_IN_01..08`, `C2_CODEC_AUX_IN`,
# `C2_PI_IN`, `C2_USB_IN`, `C2_BT_IN` — come up with `on = 0` in dsp.csv and
# are CALLED on every block regardless, at about 1,130 cycles each. With this
# on, a node whose `on` cell is 0 publishes one block of silence, raises
# `_auxin_byp_<nid>`, and the chain then skips the call entirely until the
# host turns it back on; a 0 -> 1 flip takes effect on its own block, because
# the gate's first test is the host's own cell. Six instructions per node per
# block against the ~1,130 a call costs. Block-kernel builds only.
#
# THIS LINE DID NOT EXIST UNTIL S79, AND THAT IS THE FAULT THIS FILE EXISTS
# FOR — the third time in this directory (S8-2/S9-1, then DSP4_SHARED_KERNELS
# at S76). S32 measured the switch, S33 regressed it, `shipping.config.s32`
# set it to 1 as window candidate B — and `shipping.config` never named it,
# so `build.sh:258` has defaulted it to 0 and the image that ships has been
# running the park gate OFF since 2026-09-11. S78-Q3 found it; the hub ruled
# (S79) to carry it through once its proofs were re-taken on today's pair.
#
# WHAT IT IS WORTH, re-measured on the part 2026-09-20 on the S78-fixed
# `driveall` stimulus — see MW/D24/DSP/s79/bypass.md for the full table and
# the arms' md5s.
#
# THE THIRD DIAG WORD CARRIES THIS SWITCH SINCE S80 — DIAG_BUILD_CFG3 bit 1.
# For one day it carried in no word at all: DIAG_BUILD_CFG and DIAG_BUILD_CFG2
# are full (src/diag.h says so at the point of definition), so an image with
# the park gate on and one with it off read back the SAME 0xE2018264 and a
# check that passed on one would pass on the other — S12-7's shape, which this
# project calls a defect in the instrument and not a footnote. The hub ruled
# S75's CFG3 layout (S75-13) and S80 filled it; a shipping image now reads
# 0xC47C0F26 at 0xE0EC and says the park gate is in.
DSP4_AUXIN_BYPASS=1

# ---- EVERY REMAINING SWITCH A CONFIG WORD CARRIES, NAMED (S82) ----
#
# THE FIFTH TIME. S8-2/S9-1 (block, block kernels, core clock), S11-1
# (STRIP_FUSED / SIMD_DYN), S76 (SHARED_KERNELS) and S79 (AUXIN_BYPASS) are
# all one fault: a switch that decides what ships reached the image through
# build.sh's default, and this file -- the file whose whole job is to be the
# one place the shipping configuration is written down -- said nothing about
# it. Each time it was found by accident, and each time the fix was to name
# that one switch.
#
# So the rule is now the general one, and check_shipping_config.sh ENFORCES
# it: every field DIAG_BUILD_CFG, DIAG_BUILD_CFG2 or DIAG_BUILD_CFG3 carries
# must be NAMED IN THIS FILE. Not "named if it differs from the default" --
# named, because a default that agrees today is a default that can move
# tomorrow, and the image's own config words are read back against this file.
#
# The only exemptions are the values NO configuration can set, and they are
# exempt because naming them would be a line that does not describe the
# image: DSP4_BQ_GUARD (dsp_block.h forces it to 0 under DSP4_BQ_FLOAT) and
# DSP4_GEN_BLOCK/DSP4_BLOCK_MASK/DSP4_CCLK_TARGET, which are named above.
#
# Each of these was at build.sh's default before S82 and keeps that value;
# what changes is that the file now says so, and the part's own word is
# scored against the file rather than against a default nobody read.

DSP4_GAIN_FLOAT=1         # follows DSP4_BQ_FLOAT in build.sh; stated, not derived
DSP4_GAIN_SIMD=1          # paired gain/fader stage (build.sh default since S30)
DSP4_GATHER_FIRST=1       # gather before scatter; DSP4_TX_EARLY=2 requires it
DSP4_BLOCK_DECIMATE=1     # every block profiled; >1 is a measurement arm
DSP4_BQ_SIMD_PIPE=0       # the software-pipelined paired cascade: not adopted
DSP4_C2_XPAIR=1           # chip 2's cross-chip pair ordering
DSP4_DLY_SPLIT=1          # the delay line's head window / MDMA tail split
DSP4_DYN_INLINE=2         # dynamics call depth: 2 = inlined GATE and COMP
DSP4_RTG_FABRIC=1         # the routing fabric's gathered accumulate
DSP4_FX_TYPE_DECLARED=0   # the FX engines take their type from the host
DSP4_SCOPE_BLK_TAP=0      # bench instrument only; never in a shipping image
